#
# # Rule 16 — File size and composition
#
# ## Contract
#
# This rule owns source and context-surface composition. Oversized files usually mean mixed ownership, collapsed entrypoints, hidden generated output, or logic that should move to a named helper, skill reference, or guard module.
#
# ## Budgets
#
# - Hand-written source files should stay under 500 lines unless a parser/planner table or test fixture genuinely needs more.
# - CLI entrypoints, package public entrypoints, hook runners, and MCP server entrypoints should stay thin and delegate to named modules.
# - `SKILL.md` files should stay under 500 lines. Move long details into skill-local `references/**`.
# - Rule files target 60-100 prose lines. If a rule keeps growing, split by owner or move procedure into a skill.
# - Generated files, snapshots, vendored references, benchmark evidence, and generated migration output are exempt, but must remain clearly generated or fixture-owned.
#
# ## Split decision table
#
# | Oversized source | Split toward |
# | --- | --- |
# | CLI command entrypoint | command parser + operation owner + reporter |
# | SQL planner/parser/renderer | AST/model helpers, operation-specific modules, focused tests |
# | Hook runner | thin event runner + shared check modules |
# | Guard script | detector, reporter, fixture tests, shared parser helper |
# | MCP server | tool registration + capability owner + read/search helper |
# | Docs page | concept page + command/reference page + troubleshooting page |
# | Skill | workflow in `SKILL.md`, detail in `references/**` |
#
# ## Rules
#
# - Do not split by creating generic `utils.ts`, `helpers.ts`, or catch-all shared modules.
# - Split toward real ownership: parser, planner, renderer, reporter, config, docs, hook, guard, package boundary, or MCP capability.
# - Public entrypoints stay stable and thin. Do not widen package API just to shorten a private file.
# - When extracting, update imports, tests, docs, exports, and package boundary checks in the same change.
#
# ## Verification
#
# Run owner-specific checks after composition changes. For TypeScript source, run `npm run typecheck` and the focused tests. For rule/skill/hook composition, run the relevant sync/check command and `npm run guard` when enforcement changed.
#
# ## Failure behavior
#
# If a split fails, fix imports/exports/tests in the owner surface. Do not move repo-owned source into generated output, public exports, package tarball surfaces, or docs pages just to satisfy a line budget.
#
# ## Done means
#
# - The edited file is within budget or has a clear exemption.
# - Extracted modules have real names and owners.
# - Public exports, docs, tests, and guards match the new shape.
# - No generic dump module was created.
#
